---
import AplusPage from '../../layouts/AplusPage.astro';
---
<AplusPage title="Custom Cluster Wiki | A+ Active Services" eyebrow="Wiki / custom cluster" heading="Bespoke healthcare prototypes need clear integration boundaries." intro="Custom clusters connect the tools already in use while keeping the MVP small enough to test and change.">
  <section class="aplus-screen-stack" aria-label="Custom cluster delivery model">
    <article>
      <p class="aplus-kicker">Current stack first</p>
      <h2>Healthcare Engineers start by naming the source of truth.</h2>
      <p>Before the build, we map what lives in the EHR, CRM, docs, calendar, Slack, payment system, and content engine so each integration has a job.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <p class="aplus-kicker">Last-mile plan</p>
      <h2>The prototype is not done until adoption, support, and revenue are designed.</h2>
      <p>Every custom cluster needs contracts, boundaries, human review, support ownership, compliance review, and a path from demo to the retained Healthcare Software Factory.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
  <section class="aplus-flywheel-strip" aria-label="Custom cluster boundaries">
    <span>Source of truth</span>
    <span>Contracts</span>
    <span>Boundaries</span>
    <span>Support</span>
    <span>Revenue</span>
  </section>
  <section class="aplus-content-grid">
    <article><h2>Choose the source of truth</h2><p>Decide which system owns the record, the task, the payment, and the calendar event.</p></article>
    <article><h2>Keep contracts explicit</h2><p>Document what each integration sends, receives, and refuses to touch.</p></article>
    <article><h2>Plan the last mile</h2><p>The build ends with next steps for adoption, support, compliance review, and revenue.</p></article>
  </section>
</AplusPage>
